Give the three sibling reports the json factory and construct them through it

Dev accepted, in these words: "Build the three sibling report factories in one increment" — the
recommendation being that aerial PositionReport, marine FixReport and ethereal EphemerisReport
take exactly the factory terrestrial LocationReport took in e138f04: each a drake surface
`type X from <Medium> draco format dracon Dracon` with `factory parameters par json Json`, its
JSON re-canonicalized, its hand-written companion replaced by the generator's output, its
medium's OriginateReport re-authored `fix report X X(payload)` and regenerated, and one
ReportFactoryTest in the domains package with three cases each iterating over the three.

Probed before recommending, with the compiled CLIs: each generated companion adds 27 lines to the
hand-written one and removes none — the same `apply(_json: => Json)`, Dracon-shaped encoder and
decoder, and `Null = apply(Json.Null)` LocationReport gained — and each OriginateReport regenerates
with exactly one line changed, `lazy val report: X = X(payload)`. Built as probed: three new drake
surfaces, three JSON files carrying the factory record and nothing else moved, three regenerated
companions, three OriginateReport trios re-authored on their report line. `DrakeCLI check` over
aerial, marine and ethereal: surface drift 0, json drift 0 each. No engine change. The four
OriginateReportTests already pin their Scala by exact agreement, so the regenerated rules are
gated without a test change.

ReportFactoryTest (3) is one suite, not three, because the three definitions are one pattern:
each case iterates over the three reports — exact trio agreement (emit, parse, generate, the
factory's one parameter named json typed Json, parents the medium then Dracon, the companion's
loaded definition equal to the file's); the by-name argument evaluated zero times until the first
read of `json`, once after, never again, the instance being its medium's type, Null's json being
Json.Null; and the codec round-trip for each (`asJson` is `{"json": payload}`, decoding reads the
report back, an empty object decodes to Json.Null).

With this every report in the example chain — the four media's reports and the World's Location
sink — constructs through its definition, and the thread that opened with Output's unbound
`location` on October 29 is closed. The four *Intent types share the report shape but no
definition constructs them, only tests do; they remain an observation.

